[General] The message doesn't say what was detected. Since the whole risk of this change is a false positive on a main class that happens to live under `com.sun.`/`sun.`/`jdk.`, "JDK tool detected" gives a user hitting one nothing to correlate against, and it's the only output they get before the agent goes quiet.

Returning the detected command instead of a boolean keeps it to two small edits — here:

```java
    String jdkToolCommand = fromPremain ? jdkToolCommand() : null;
    if (jdkToolCommand != null) {
      System.err.println(
          "JDK tool detected ("
              + jdkToolCommand
              + "), agent will not be started. To override this behavior, set"
              + " otel.javaagent.enabled=true as an agent argument or system property, or"
              + " OTEL_JAVAAGENT_ENABLED=true as an environment variable");
      return;
    }
```

and in the helper:

```java
  @Nullable
  private static String jdkToolCommand() {
    // ... unchanged comment ...
    return doPrivileged(
        new PrivilegedAction<String>() {
          @Override
          @Nullable
          public String run() {
            String enable = System.getProperty("otel.javaagent.enabled");
            if (enable == null) {
              enable = System.getenv("OTEL_JAVAAGENT_ENABLED");
            }
            if (Boolean.parseBoolean(enable)) {
              return null;
            }
            String cmd = System.getProperty("sun.java.command");
            return isJdkToolMainClass(cmd) ? cmd : null;
          }
        });
  }
```

